## Context

Author standing rule: render the PDF and adjust table column widths after
any table change. The reading-3 arm-3 column (0628) made `tbl:status-difficulty`
158pt overfull (5 columns, two ~28-char headers "Avg. detection prob. (Exp 1)"
/ "(Exp 2, 1D)").

## Actions (done)

- Shortened the EN headers in the emitter `src/aedist/tabulate_status_difficulty.py`:
  "Avg. detection prob. (Exp 1)" -> "Detection (Exp 1)"; "Share of list" -> "Share".
  Regenerated `tab_status_difficulty_en.tex`.
- Wrapped the table `\input` in `{\small\setlength{\tabcolsep}{4pt}...}` in main.tex.
- Result: overfull 158pt -> 0 (gone). Manuscript builds.
- Loosened the over-pinned header test `test_status_en_header_matches_detection_framing`
  (it asserted the exact old phrasing — a CI-polarity violation): now pins the
  stable markers "(Exp 1)"/"(Exp 2, 1D)" + "detection" + the "Recognition rate"
  negative guard, not the exact wording.

## Verification
- [x] No status-difficulty overfull \hbox; manuscript builds.
- [x] Header test passes (loosened, polarity-compliant).
- [ ] `make check` passes.

## Exit criteria
- status-difficulty table fits; header test polarity-compliant; build clean.
